# The Body Model and body parts


<!-- ================================================================== -->
## Models of body-part

The body model is a complex structure that consists of various body parts, each represented by its own model.
This structure arise from historical and practical reasons, where each body part is modeled separately,
for instance due to data availability, anatomical considerations, or specific functional requirements. 
This modular approach allows for detailed analysis and simulation of each body part while maintaining 
a coherent overall body model. 
And it also allows for development of new models of body parts replacing or supplementing existing ones in parallel.


AMMR's body model is organized into the following main components, i.e. body-parts and sub-body-parts:

- Trunk model
  - Lumbar spine model
  - Thoracical (and rib cage) spine
  - Cervical spine model
  - Abdominal model
- Leg model
  - Foot model
- Arm (Arm-Shoulder)
  - Hand model

  
